    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **53 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership level 4 in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`).\n\nThe pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for zero namesakes) are still capped at 3. On top of that cap, level 4 is now reached by adding 1 when the owner's **tenure \u2014 days between `registrationDate` and today \u2014 exceeds 365**:\n\n```java\nlevel = Math.min(level, 3);\nif (this.registrationDate != null\n        && ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365) {\n    level += 1;\n}\nreturn level;\n```\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is the creation date, its tenure is 0, so the tenure factor never applies at creation \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` of 0, and a 3-member household lands at level 3, exactly as the spec (and `Cp39Tests`) requires. I also updated the Javadoc to document the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule.",
